1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,050
Listen to a talk in an art history class.

2
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:06,518
Man:

3
00:00:06,518 --> 00:00:12,010
When we think of the Renaissance, we often picture grand paintings and sculptures.

4
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:18,100
But a lesser known art form also flourished during this period—tapestry weaving.

5
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,972
Tapestries were not only decorative pieces,

6
00:00:20,972 --> 00:00:28,000
but also served practical purposes, such as insulating the cold stone walls of castles.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,224
Artists of the era used tapestries to depict intricate scenes from mythology, religion,

8
00:00:35,224 --> 00:00:40,260
and daily life, often incorporating vibrant colors and rich textures.

9
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:44,100
An advantage of tapestries was their portability.

10
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,624
Unlike frescoes,

11
00:00:45,624 --> 00:00:48,952
which were fixed to walls, tapestries could be rolled up

12
00:00:48,952 --> 00:00:56,210
and transported from one location to another, allowing their owners to display their wealth wherever they went.

13
00:00:56,210 --> 00:01:00,065
This portability also had a downside, however.

14
00:01:00,065 --> 00:01:04,080
Tapestries were susceptible to damage during transit.

15
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:12,020
Even today, museums face challenges preserving these unique artworks due to their fragile nature.

16
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:22,010
The creation of a tapestry was a labor-intensive process requiring collaboration between designers, weavers, and dyers.

17
00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:23,017
Unlike paintings,

18
00:01:23,017 --> 00:01:29,060
which could be completed by a single artist, tapestries were team efforts.

19
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:36,070
And it was common for a designer's sketches to be translated by skilled weavers into woven masterpieces.

20
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:44,212
The intricate craftsmanship required to produce these artworks offers a glimpse into the collaborative

21
00:01:44,212 --> 00:01:47,120
spirit of the Renaissance era.
